# =============================================================================
# Copy to .env and REPLACE every placeholder. Do not commit .env.
#   copy .env.example .env
# Checklist:  powershell -File scripts\print-env-checklist.ps1
# Full Neon steps: see README.md "Neon setup" or Project store docs/neon-setup.md
# =============================================================================

# --- Postgres (REQUIRED) ---
# Prisma P1001 = wrong/unreachable host. The literal host "HOST" is a PLACEHOLDER.
# Get a real URL from https://console.neon.tech → your project → Connect
# (use the pooled or direct connection string Neon shows; keep ?sslmode=require).
#
# REAL shape (example only — replace USER, PASSWORD, ep-xxx…, and db name):
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@ep-xxxxxxxx.us-east-2.aws.neon.tech/neondb?sslmode=require"
#
# Local Postgres alternative (only if you run Postgres yourself):
# DATABASE_URL="postgresql://postgres:postgres@127.0.0.1:5432/strata?schema=public"

# --- Better Auth (REQUIRED) ---
# Must be at least 32 characters. Generate one of:
#   openssl rand -base64 32
#   node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('base64'))"
# Do NOT leave the short placeholder below — Better Auth will warn/fail.
BETTER_AUTH_SECRET="PASTE_OUTPUT_OF_openssl_rand_base64_32_HERE_MIN_32_CHARS"

# Public origin of this app. No trailing slash.
# Resolution (see src/lib/app-origin.ts):
#   1. BETTER_AUTH_URL / NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL if set (explicit override / custom domain)
#   2. else https://${VERCEL_URL} on Vercel (VERCEL_URL is injected automatically; no protocol in the raw var)
#   3. else http://localhost:3000 for local
# On Vercel you can omit both URL vars and rely on VERCEL_URL. Set BETTER_AUTH_URL
# only when using a custom domain. Local: keep localhost and open that URL in the browser.
# Opening http://192.168.x.x:3000 while these stay on localhost used to break sign-in
# (cross-origin client + untrusted Origin). Auth client is now same-origin; server
# trusts loopback/LAN Origins in development. Prefer localhost anyway.
BETTER_AUTH_URL="http://localhost:3000"
NEXT_PUBLIC_APP_URL="http://localhost:3000"
# Optional comma-separated extras (Better Auth reads this automatically):
# BETTER_AUTH_TRUSTED_ORIGINS="http://192.168.1.10:3000"

#
# Rotating BETTER_AUTH_SECRET does NOT invalidate password hashes (scrypt, independent).
# It does invalidate signed session cookies — clear site cookies for localhost / your LAN host.

# --- AI (optional, free tiers) — see docs/ai-providers.md ---
# Set any combination. At runtime Strata tries in order Groq → Google → OpenRouter
# and falls back to the next configured key if a request throws or returns an error.
# Defaults below are current free/developer-tier IDs (Oct 2026). Remove stale
# GROQ_MODEL / GOOGLE_AI_MODEL / OPENROUTER_MODEL overrides in Vercel if set.
# GROQ_API_KEY=
# GROQ_MODEL=openai/gpt-oss-20b
# GOOGLE_GENERATIVE_AI_API_KEY=
# GOOGLE_AI_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite
# OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
# OPENROUTER_MODEL=openrouter/free

# Local attachment blobs land in ./uploads (gitignored). Max 8 MB per file.
